==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Good for grinding (No M1 dash).
* M1 attacks are really fast, which makes it a pretty good choice for grinding with [[Buddha]].
* Low cooldown.
* Good mobility.
* Very little casting time. (No start-up)
* Both attacks can damage [[Sea Beasts]].
* High skill ceiling.
* Great combo potential when mastered.

|'''[Z] Death Cyclone'''
* Very large hitbox.
* Very high stun.
* Drains 4 instinct dodges.

|'''[X] Soul Execution'''
* Good mobility.
* Deals 1.2x more damage if the enemy is below 50% [[Health|HP]].
* [[Breaks Instinct]].
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Hard to obtain, due to the drop chances being low and [[Hallow Essence]] having a low chance to obtain.
* High mastery requirements.
* Lowest M1 damage compared to other {{Mythical}} swords, so it is recommended to use another {{Mythical}} sword if the player uses [[Buddha]] unless they do not have any.
* Difficult to master.

|'''[Z] Death Cyclone'''
* Hard to grind with.
* High knockback (if the player uses [[Buddha]], they can shoot the tornado down and spam left clicks).
* Easy to [[Instinct]] trick.

|'''[X] Soul Execution'''
* Hard to land.
* Short range.
* Slow move.
* Small hitbox.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* The Hallow Scythe is the first [[sword]] to have a unique mechanic.
** The less [[health]] the opponent has, the more damage the player will do with [X].
* The Hallow Scythe was once used to kill admin [[Uzoth (Player)|Uzoth]]. In this [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N1xEFc38Oo0 video], a player used a combo with [[Portal]]'s Pre-nerfed [C] to teleport the admin into the [[lava]] in [[Hot and Cold]], then dragged them into it using the sword’s [Z] move, resulting in an instant kill.
* The engravings on the blade of the scythe mean "Death", while the engravings on the tang of the scythe "風間" can be read as Kazama in Japanese, meaning "Between Wind". Both the engravings combined make the word "Death Between Wind", alluding to Death Cyclone.
* The Hallow Scythe is used by the Lv. 2100 [[Raid Bosses|Raid Boss]], [[Soul Reaper]].
* The Burning [[Enchantments|blessing]] does not visually appear on Hallow Scythe.
* The Hallow scythe has the same holding animation as the [[Shark Anchor]].

